##source=logan-walker intra-host SNPs. Frequencies are k-mer coverage (ka:f) ratios at a graph fork, a proxy for allele frequency, not read counts. Sites are per-locus and NOT phased: two rows do not assert co-occurrence on one molecule, UNLESS they share a BLOCK, which means one alternative haplotype carries both. ka:f is clipped at 25000, and a row whose fork reaches it is FILTERed KaSat with an overstated AF.
